From e1e9c32531c1fabfc2a32fe50c1997972a60c04e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naiwen Yu <naiwyu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:33:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lat_rpc: fix SIGSEGV caused by uninitialized state.server in -S path

In the '-S <host>' (shutdown) case, when clnt_create() fails,
clnt_pcreateerror() is called with state.server which has not been
initialized yet.

The garbage pointer value may be passed as a %s argument to snprintf 
inside clnt_spcreateerror(), causing strlen() to dereference an invalid
address and crash with SIGSEGV.

The server hostname is already available in optarg at this point (set by
getopt for the -S option), so use that instead.

Backtrace from coredump:
  #7 main (lat_rpc.c:116)        clnt_pcreateerror(state.server)  <- uninitialized
  #6 clnt_pcreateerror()
  #5 clnt_spcreateerror()
  #4 snprintf(..., "%s: ", s)     s = 0xffff00000000
  #0 __strlen_generic()           SIGSEGV

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate

Signed-off-by: Naiwen Yu <naiwyu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/lat_rpc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lat_rpc.c b/src/lat_rpc.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/lat_rpc.c
+++ b/src/lat_rpc.c
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ main(int ac, char **av)
 		case 'S': /* shutdown serverhost */
 		{
 			cl = clnt_create(optarg, XACT_PROG, XACT_VERS, "udp");
 			if (!cl) {
-				clnt_pcreateerror(state.server);
+				clnt_pcreateerror(optarg);
 				exit(1);
 			}
